  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "English is the existing vocabulary and the lingua franca of institutional labels; Lithuanian and Russian are included because they are the languages this plugin's operator audits and reports in. Those three vocabularies have been reviewed by a person. The /datenschutz href fragment is an inherited ad-hoc entry, kept in en because removing it would change behaviour; it should move when German is added properly. Credential and first_hand terms match body prose, so a page that merely quotes an expert can receive the same credit that English expert has always given; the non-English lists mirror that weakness, and fixing it requires grading where a credential appears as separate work. Adding another language is data rather than code, but its terms must be reviewed before inclusion. The `contact` family (0.116.0) holds only terms `trust` already carried, so it adds no word that review has not seen.",
